.TH FINDER-LINUX 1 "2026-11-14" "Finder 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
finder-linux \- macOS Finder-inspired file manager for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B finder-linux
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATH\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Finder Linux
is a native Qt 6 file manager with icon, list, column, and gallery views,
Quick Look previews, split-pane browsing, XDG Trash support, archive management,
and freedesktop.org/KDE desktop integration.
.PP
When launched without arguments it opens the configured default folder.
Multiple paths are opened as separate tabs. If an instance is already running,
the paths are forwarded to it unless
.B \-\-new\-window
is used.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-select " " \fITARGET\fR
Open the containing folder of
.I TARGET
and select that item.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-new\-window
Open a new window even if Finder is already running.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Display command-line help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open the current user's home folder:
.EX
finder-linux
.EE
.TP
Open a folder in a new tab in an existing instance:
.EX
finder-linux /path/to/folder
.EE
.TP
Open a folder and select a file inside it:
.EX
finder-linux \-\-select /path/to/folder/document.pdf
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/FinderLinux/FinderLinux.conf
Persistent application settings.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/recently-used.xbel
Shared freedesktop.org recent-files database.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Trash
XDG Trash location.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg-open (1),
.BR gio (1),
.BR dolphin (1),
.BR ark (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Finder Linux contributors
